  "reason": "Evidence: The largest performance jump in the study came from switching to multiprofile (config_018: 0.619 vs config_016: 0.527 for multimodal; config_002: 0.591 vs config_001: 0.485 for RNA-only), and the only aggregation tested so far is avgpool. Fusion method (concat vs weighted) showed negligible difference in singleprofile (0.527 vs 0.523), so it is lower priority. Question: Does transformer aggregation outperform avgpool for combining multiple profiles, given that the multiprofile gain is the dominant source of accuracy? This experiment (config_020) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other parameters at their current best values (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat), cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why best next: It is a single-variable extension of the current best configuration, directly tests whether a more expressive aggregation can further exploit the multiprofile signal, and the result will inform whether transformer aggregation is worth exploring across other encoder/fusion combinations under the limited budget."
}

